course: dictionary
lesson: 9963
title: Words with two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A taxi is usually a car with a driver that you pay to take you somewhere. «London taxi drivers who learned all the streets were found to have a bigger memory area.» Here taxi drivers means the people who drive those cars.
explain: The same word can also be an action word, called a verb. When a plane taxis, it moves slowly along the ground before it takes off or after it lands. Look at the words around the word to find which meaning fits: a car with a driver, or a plane on the ground.
explain: Check your choice by swapping in your meaning. «Jayden said that in GTA 6 you can fly to the Moon in a taxi.» Flying to the Moon is not something a plane on the ground does, so the words around taxi show it means a car with a driver, a made-up ride in a game.
fact: A taxi is a car with a driver that you pay to take you where you want to go.
fact: People take a taxi or call a taxi when they need a ride, and they can wait at a taxi rank.
fact: A taxi fare is often shown on a meter, and maths problems can use a starting charge plus a price per kilometre or mile.
fact: When a plane taxis, it moves slowly along the ground before taking off or after landing.
fact: Children should not take a taxi alone; adults should use licensed taxis.
exercise: «London taxi drivers who learned all the streets were found to have a bigger memory area.» What is a taxi driver? | *A person who drives a taxi, the car you pay to ride in | A map of London streets | A person who sells tickets at the station | A plane that moves along the runway
exercise: When a plane taxis, what does it do? | It drives people across the sea | It flies very high above the clouds | *It moves slowly along the ground before taking off | It waits at a taxi rank for passengers
exercise: Which phrase means a place where taxis wait for passengers? | *taxi rank | taxi fare | taxi driver | taxi plane
test: A taxi costs 3 pounds to start, then 2 pounds for each kilometre. How much does a 4 kilometre ride cost? | 7 pounds | 12 pounds | 8 pounds | *11 pounds
test: Which sentence uses taxi as an action word? | Our taxi rank is near the station. | *The plane will taxi slowly to the gate. | The taxi driver waved at us. | We took a taxi home from school.
exam: In «It turned out that Jayden had made up the Moon taxi to impress everyone», what does made up mean? | Paid for in full | Cooked for a meal | *Invented, so it was not real | Driven very fast
